6. Resources for research and content
I'd use these as your primary research sources rather than relying on random blogs.

1. NOAA – Geodetic Leveling
Highly recommended
Detailed explanations of geodetic leveling, benchmarks, orthometric heights and measurement procedures.
Read NOAA documentation



2. Geodetic Leveling Manual

A comprehensive technical manual covering leveling procedures, equipment, benchmarks and measurement errors.
Read the technical manual (PDF)



3. NOAA – Vertical Datums

Useful for understanding vertical reference systems and different types of elevation.
Explore vertical datums



4. USDA – Surveying Handbook

Contains explanations and diagrams of differential leveling, turning points, backsight and foresight.
Read surveying chapter



5. North Carolina Geodetic Survey

Useful illustrations explaining differential and trigonometric leveling.
Explore leveling diagrams (PDF)


One important thing: These are international references, not necessarily the official vertical reference system used in North Macedonia. For the local section, try to obtain information about the Macedonian national height reference system from the Agency for Real Estate Cadastre (Агенција за катастар на недвижности).
